theorem an-order-claimed-with-an-identity
  note        The claim writes y/1 to the power 1, which is y with its
              identity elements dropped, and the rows end on x ≤ y.
  let x ∈ ℝ                                                           (H1)
  let y ∈ ℝ                                                           (H2)
  assume x = y                                                        (H3)
  then x ≤ (y/1)^1

1.  x ≤ (y/1)^1
    inequalities
      x = y          H3
      x ≤ y          weakening
